# 低频词汇 List02
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List02核心词汇

blunt /blʌnt/ adj./v. 钝的；使迟钝 His blunt manner offended some people. 他直率的态度冒犯了一些人。
boast /bəʊst/ v./n. 吹嘘 He boasted about his achievements. 他吹嘘自己的成就。
brace /breɪs/ v./n. 支撑；准备 The city braced for the approaching hurricane. 该城市为即将到来的飓风做好了准备。
brisk /brɪsk/ adj. 活跃的；轻快的 Business has been brisk this quarter. 本季度生意一直很活跃。
bulk /bʌlk/ n. 大部分；体积 The bulk of the work has been completed. 大部分工作已经完成。
bypass /ˈbaɪpɑːs/ v./n. 绕过；旁路 We can bypass the traffic by taking a different route. 我们可以走另一条路线绕过交通。
calibrate /ˈkælɪbreɪt/ v. 校准 The instruments need to be calibrated regularly. 仪器需要定期校准。
canopy /ˈkænəpi/ n. 树冠；顶篷 The trees formed a dense canopy overhead. 树木在头顶形成了茂密的树冠。
cascade /kæˈskeɪd/ n./v. 瀑布；级联 The policy had a cascade effect on the economy. 该政策对经济产生了连锁反应。
catalyst /ˈkætəlɪst/ n. 催化剂；促进因素 The protest was a catalyst for change. 抗议是变革的催化剂。
census /ˈsensəs/ n. 人口普查 The census is conducted every ten years. 人口普查每十年进行一次。
certify /ˈsɜːtɪfaɪ/ v. 证明 The document was certified by a notary. 文件由公证人认证。
charter /ˈtʃɑːtə(r)/ n./v. 宪章；包租 The United Nations Charter promotes peace. 联合国宪章促进和平。
choir /ˈkwaɪə(r)/ n. 合唱团 The school choir performed at the concert. 学校合唱团在音乐会上演出。
cite /saɪt/ v. 引用 The article cited several recent studies. 文章引用了几项最近的研究。
clamp /klæmp/ v./n. 夹紧；限制 The government clamped down on tax evasion. 政府严厉打击逃税。
clan /klæn/ n. 宗族；氏族 The clan has lived in this region for centuries. 这个氏族在这个地区生活了几个世纪。
clergy /ˈklɜːdʒi/ n. 神职人员 The clergy played an important role in the community. 神职人员在社区中扮演了重要角色。
clone /kləʊn/ n./v. 克隆 Scientists successfully cloned the animal. 科学家成功克隆了这种动物。
cluster /ˈklʌstə(r)/ n./v. 群；聚集 The houses were built in clusters. 房屋成群建造。
coalition /ˌkəʊəˈlɪʃn/ n. 联盟 The two parties formed a coalition government. 两党组成了联合政府。
coexist /ˌkəʊɪɡˈzɪst/ v. 共存 Different cultures can coexist peacefully. 不同文化可以和平共存。
coherent /kəʊˈhɪərənt/ adj. 连贯的 The argument must be coherent and logical. 论点必须连贯且有逻辑。
commemorate /kəˈmeməreɪt/ v. 纪念 The ceremony commemorates the end of the war. 这个仪式纪念战争的结束。
commence /kəˈmens/ v. 开始 Construction will commence next month. 建设将于下月开始。
compatible /kəmˈpætəbl/ adj. 兼容的 The two systems are not compatible. 这两个系统不兼容。
compile /kəmˈpaɪl/ v. 编辑 She compiled a list of all the references. 她编辑了一份所有参考文献的清单。
complementary /ˌkɒmplɪˈmentəri/ adj. 互补的 The two approaches are complementary. 这两种方法是互补的。
comply /kəmˈplaɪ/ v. 遵守 All employees must comply with the safety regulations. 所有员工必须遵守安全规定。
concede /kənˈsiːd/ v. 承认；让步 He conceded that he had made a mistake. 他承认自己犯了一个错误。
